    "lawCode": "Amd §10, Munic Home R L",
    "lawSection": "Municipal Home Rule Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8272A\n\nSPONSOR: GALLIVAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the municipal home rule law, in relation to punishment\nfor the violation of a local law\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide for community service as one of the punishments regarding a\nviolation of a local law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill codifies as a means of punishment for violating a\nlocal law the ability to perform community service. Such community\nservice must not result in the displacement of employed workers or in\nthe impairment of existing services, nor shall the performance of any\nsuch services be required or permitted in any establishment involved in\nany labor strike or lockout.\n\nSection 2 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nState law prescribes the type of punishment, which may be imposed by a\nmunicipality, pursuant to local law, to include a civil penalty, fine,\nforfeiture or imprisonment. This legislation will add to the type of\npunishment, community service for a violation of a local law as well.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-18: A.5539A - referred to local governments\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis Act shall take effect immediately.\n",
